### How to build your trees
- **No worktree is created in the NexusAI repo, and you never work in its `2_Project_Files` checkout or any builder `worktrees/` directory** (S87N's `worktrees/s87n-rd640`, `worktrees/s87n-rd697`). In that repo use ONLY read verbs: `show`, `diff`, `log`, `ls-tree`, `cat-file`, `grep`, `ls-remote`, `rev-parse`, `merge-base`, `rev-list` (plus `count-objects` for §7.9). **NEVER `fetch`, `pull`, `push`, `checkout`, `worktree`, `commit`, `stash`, `gc`, `merge`; and `merge-tree --write-tree` ONLY with `GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY=<your own scratch dir> GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES=<repo>/.git/objects`.**
- **Every tree is K1** — `git clone --shared --no-checkout <repo> <dir>` then `checkout` in YOUR clone (origin removed; local identity; `gc.auto 0`; `core.fsmonitor false`; hooks off), under a fresh `mktemp -d` in `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/!CODING/Testing Agent MAIN/projects/nexusai/qa-trees/batch17.XXXXXX/`. Status-check before use.
- **Each tree is EXCLUSIVE to this gate and to ONE purpose.** A fresh arm per mutant; never reuse a mutant tree for a clean arm; `batch17`-prefixed directories only. **Gates 14's and 15's trees (`qa-trees/batch14.*`, `qa-trees/batch15.*`) are LIVE peers' — never run in them, never write to them, never clone node_modules FROM them** (nor from gates 12/13/16's).
