## 9. Floor discipline — THE FOUR CLAUSES, plus MERGES GO FIRST and THE DEADLINE RULE
1. **MERGES GO FIRST (ruling i).** **The jest lock `session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh` (queue `session-tools/locks/queue-jest/`) is shared with gates 14 and 15 (`qa-b14-`, `qa-b15-` tags, LIVE) and the builder seats** (at 06:23:30 the queue held `s89r-rd761-hold01`, `s87n-merge-rd648`, `qa-b14-H6`, `s87n-rd791-hold`, `s86m-rd756-hold` — READ).
   - **Do ALL lock-free work first:** pins, reads, merge-trees in scratch objects, the offline `npm ci` (H-31), the plain-node rows (a2-a5, a7, a8, b4), census greps, prior-work reads, CI reads.
   - **Then file your holds (H-28), ONE AT A TIME**, each tagged `qa-b17-…` (e.g. `qa-b17-H1`), each a tracked child of your seat. **If a MERGE ticket (a tag containing `merge`) is queued AHEAD of you, you wait behind it (that is FIFO). If a MERGE ticket FILES BEHIND YOU BEFORE YOUR HOLD IS GRANTED, re-file your ticket behind it:** stop YOUR OWN unstarted waiter (its ancestry proven to reach your claude pid — C-174: by pid, never by pattern), confirm your ticket went to `released/` as `ticket-left-*`, and re-queue with `--after <that merge ticket's tag>` (C-141 ADDENDUM 4's tool) **under your UNCHANGED tag** (ADDENDUM 5). **At a wait deadline while FIRST in line: ruling (i)'s replace-then-withdraw.** Record each re-file with its place before and after FROM THE QUEUE LISTING (gate 16 S-6). **Once your hold is GRANTED, carry on** — a running hold is never interrupted; **between holds, re-file behind any merge ticket.** Gates 14's and 15's tickets are PEER gates': FIFO, never re-filed around, never touched.
   - C-141: your hold is gate-class; builder PROOF tickets self-apply ONE yield per gate TAG. **QUEUE, NEVER TAKE OVER:** never kill, signal, move or edit another seat's process, lock directory, owner file or ticket, even if it looks stuck; if a holder looks stuck, mail a QUESTION (§11) and keep waiting. **Known lock-tool message (RELAYED by builders):** `nexusai-lock.sh: line 241: …/nexusai-jest.lock/owner: No such file or directory` at acquire, then a normal grant — record it if you see it.
2. **Hold the lock for a planned block of work, never idle (H-28)** — at most ~40 minutes of planned jest per hold, one hold at a time. Every hold is a TRACKED CHILD of your seat, never detached (`nohup … &`).
3. **Count foreign servers the C-125 way, anchored on YOUR OWN claude pid:** `basename(argv[0]) == node` AND the server entry point anywhere in the remaining argv; "ours" = the ancestor chain CONTAINS your own claude pid. **Record the foreign count BESIDE EVERY RESULT.** **NEGATIVE controls, all in the same run, all must classify FOREIGN: the claude pids of the LIVE cockpit panes among `Datasec/NexusAI-M`, `-N`, `-O`, `-P`, `-R` and the coordinator pane `tuesday`, DERIVED LIVE by the launcher at launch and listed at the end of your prompt** (and the claudes of gates 14 and 15, if their panes are live). This brief names no pids: they change with every restart. Re-read them at the start of every hold; if one has exited, say so and use the others; **a hold with NO live negative control aborts.** Reuse gate 16's instrument BY COPY with YOUR pid as `ROOT` and these as `NEG` (`qa-floorlib16.sh`, its defaults STALE — correct `ROOT` and `NEG` before any hold) and `…/qa-floorcount.py`. Count every child you start and prove 0 left after each run (H-33).
4. **A zero is reportable only beside a control that fired in the same window** — the floor count, "target unchanged" (a3's modified copy detected), "kept, not purged" (M-anyNull purges it), "no needle" (a8's planted copy found), "no reason line" (a5's dangling arm prints it), "LOST 0", "missing 0", "guarded by no cell" (the mutant LANDED and parsed).

**5. THE DEADLINE RULE — every probe, every child and every request has a per-step DEADLINE, a HEARTBEAT, and kills its child in a `finally`.**
Each step (offline npm ci 600 s, node driver 120 s, purge/re-drive process 120 s, targeted jest 600 s, C-68 union 1,800 s, full verify 2,400 s, exit 25 s) has a written DEADLINE (`qa-to.sh`); a step past it is ABORTED and reported, never waited on. **Log a HEARTBEAT line at least every 2 minutes during any hold (H-4: a separate child, ≤ 120 s max gap, aborted if absent at 90 s); a step with no heartbeat for 5 minutes is aborted and reported,** and a hold that is not progressing releases the lock. Every process and child you start is killed in a `finally` (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after a grace) **by pid from your own ancestry, never by pattern (C-174)**, and the reap is confirmed by your floor counter. **H-20 and H-21 apply to every jest.**

